<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Stucco repair in Northwest Calgary mostly means houses from the 1990s and 2000s. The City of Calgary labels Citadel, Edgemont, Hawkwood and Scenic Acres as 1980s and 1990s communities, and Arbour Lake, Hamptons, Rocky Ridge and Tuscany as 2000s ones. By those labels, many of the walls here have been through well over a decade of Calgary winters.</p><p>Sandstone Stucco Co is an advertising and introduction service. It puts you in touch with independent stucco contractors who quote and contract directly with you, and it is paid by those contractors. Read the <a href="/stucco-repair-calgary/">stucco repair overview</a> for how it works, then call (403) 555-0148 or send the form to describe your wall.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Northwest Calgary</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Northwest Calgary Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Cracks, patches and colour matching</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Chips, hairline cracks and small patches. Calgary Parging lists $550 to $1,125 before GST for small patch repairs, and says colour matching can add $230 to $575. On a weathered finish a perfect match may not be possible.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Hail and flicker damage</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hail pocking and holes drilled by northern flickers, looked at on the wall itself. Calgary Parging lists a typical single-woodpecker patch with reinforcement at $600 to $800 (GST not stated). A contractor can put hail damage in a written estimate you may give your insurer.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Foundation parging</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Recoating and patching the cement coat at the base of the wall. Calgary Parging lists $975 to $1,700 before GST to recoat one side of a house. This is surface coating only; a crack in the foundation itself is a question for a foundation specialist.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Re-stucco and recoat</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Larger areas, or a whole elevation, when a patch will not do. Martini Stone Masonry lists $14,350 before GST for one elevation stripped to the face and refinished in acrylic. Whether repair or replacement fits is the contractor's call after seeing the wall.</p>
      </div>
</div>
